@startuml
title ProofSieve · Author, test and activate a rule
hide footbox

actor Administrator as Admin
participant "Guard UI" as UI
participant "Guard API" as API
participant "Saved rules\n(JSON state)" as Rules

Admin -> UI: Sign in with an admin token
UI -> API: GET /auth/me
API --> UI: Admin identity, endpoint grants and editor token

alt Edit an existing writable endpoint
    Admin -> UI: Select a granted /verify/... path
    UI -> API: GET /admin/rule?endpoint=...
    API -> Rules: Read current rule
    API --> UI: Saved rule and ETag
else Create an endpoint
    Admin -> UI: Enter a permitted /verify/... path
end

alt ODRL
    Admin -> UI: Edit nested conditions in the graph or JSON-LD
    Admin -> UI: Apply or discard pending condition edits
    UI -> UI: Sync the graph and supported JSON-LD draft
else SHACL
    Admin -> UI: Edit Turtle shapes in the text editor
end
Admin -> UI: Choose the response mode and edit its options

opt Test the draft in the dialog
    Admin -> UI: Paste or load input\nRun document checks explicitly with the saved profile
    UI -> API: POST /admin/test-rule?endpoint=...\nDraft rule and test input
    API -> API: Check admin grant and editor token\nEvaluate the draft using configured checks
    API --> UI: Decision preview and available rule trace
    note over UI, API
      The preview evaluates the input on the server.
      Live forwarding and decision evidence are tied to POST /verify/...
    end note
end

opt Activate the draft
    Admin -> UI: Save rule
    UI -> API: PUT /admin/rule?endpoint=...\nIf-Match for edits, If-None-Match: * for creation
    API -> API: Check admin grant, editor token and rule
    alt Save condition holds
        API -> Rules: Store and activate the rule
        API --> UI: Saved rule and new ETag
    else Stale edit or path already exists
        API --> UI: HTTP 412 · Reload and reconcile
    end
end
@enduml
